 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6023+) **Barbarian global city spawning no longer applies normal-civilization distance shaping:** ordinary civilizations expand from their existing empire, while Barbarian cities are selected from a global map scan. In save file 450, this normal-civ distance rule could hard-reject locally strong Barbarian candidates such as `70,37`, so Barbarian placement now skips that rule. See [KI#177](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#177---fixed-multiple-base-advcivk-mod-barbarian-city-placement-issues-could-produce-poor-captured-city-sites).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6023+) **Rejected Barbarian sites stay rejected after area-priority adjustment:** in save file 450, the later area-priority adjustment could turn raw rejected sites such as `30,23` back into valid spawns. AdvCiv-SAS now skips raw rejected Barbarian candidates before area adjustment, and the BBAI diagnostics log raw, area-adjusted, and final chooser values so these cases are visible. See [KI#177](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#177---fixed-multiple-base-advcivk-mod-barbarian-city-placement-issues-could-produce-poor-captured-city-sites).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6025+) **Barbarian city sites now value bonus health/happiness too:** Base AdvCiv skipped Barbarian non-yield bonus value because Barbarians do not care about ordinary bonus trading. AdvCiv-SAS instead values Barbarian-founded cities as real long-term city sites: Barbarians benefit from better cities, and players often later capture them. In save file 450 BBAI testing, the Barbarian Hittite site at `(13,35)` now scored nearby Crab with explicit `happyHealth=300 buildingHappyHealth=150`, so seafood health and ordinary building effects help Barbarian placement too. See [KI#178](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#178---fixedimproved-city-site-bonus-valuation-used-broad-trade-style-ai_bonusval-instead-of-settlement-specific-long-term-value).
